n    parent: mvp_001\n    spec:\n      command: python harness.py --clauses clause_templates_diag001.json --models\n        gpt-5.4,gpt-4.1 --output results_diag001\n      server: localhost\n      data_path: artifacts/clause_templates_diag001.json\n      data_count: 200\n      model_name: gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1\n      seed: N/A (API sampling)\n      design: 2 types (CP 50 + scopal 50) x 2 conditions x 2 models = 400 episodes\n      endpoint: http://47.94.22.126/v1\n      checkpoint_source: N/A (API models, no checkpoint)\n      eval_data: clause_templates_diag001.json (50 CP + 50 scopal matched pairs)\n      checkpoint_path: artifacts/results_diag001/\n      log_path: artifacts/analysis_diag001/\n      metrics:\n        violation_rate_cp_ambig: 0.34\n        violation_rate_scopal_ambig: 0.4\n        violation_rate_cp_unambig: 0.03\n        violation_rate_scopal_unambig: 0.03\n        cp_vs_scopal_delta_pp: -6\n        fisher_exact_p: 0.4641\n        odds_ratio: 0.773\n        ambiguity_effect_cp: 0.31\n        ambiguity_effect_scopal: 0.37\n    conclusion: negative\n    completed_at: '2026-05-20T11:23:41.300Z'\n  plan_002:\n    status: DONE\n    retry_count: 0\n    created_at: '2026-05-20T15:16:08.165Z'\n    updated_at: '2026-05-20T15:16:42.586Z'\n    hypothesis: Policy ambiguity causes significantly higher agent safety violation\n      rates (+30-40pp) across all 6 ambiguity types, with uniform effect size across\n      types (no significant type×violation interaction). Binary effect is the primary\n      finding; type uniformity supports that ambiguity per se, not specific linguistic\n      structures, drives violations.\n    spec:\n      command: python run_full_study.py --all --clauses clause_templates_full.json\n        --models gpt-5.4,gpt-4.1 --concurrency 10\n      server: local (API experiment)\n      data_path: artifacts/clause_templates_full.json\n      data_count: 300\n      model_name: gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1\n      seed: N/A\n      checkpoint_path: artifacts/full_s